From 58d101f9df24c8d812b28477f604632f9080e59a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adaeze Okonkwo <adaeze.okonkwo@example.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:17:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(billing): change the monthly spend limit from /topup

The Monthly limit screen was read-only and sent admins to the portal.
Portal now accepts PUT /api/billing/monthly-cap from billing:manage
tokens, so admins with Remote Spending on can set the limit here:

- MonthlyCap carries ceilingUsd (the highest limit the org may set).
- validate_monthly_limit mirrors the endpoint's accept/reject for
  instant feedback; the server stays authoritative.
- nous_billing.put_monthly_cap sends limitUsd as a JSON number.
- The screen prompts for the new limit, notes when it lands below
  this month's spend, and reuses the scope step-up and error copy.

_billing_patch_auto_top_up becomes _billing_mutate(state, call, ...)
so auto-reload and the limit share one scope/error path.
